@*
    The money that moved. Net deltas only — splitting them into the round payment and the
    money-card side bet needs the ownership record, which is on the table and not in the
    result (BUILD-PLAN P8). The console has the table; a watcher has what it was told, and it
    is told the nets.

    🔥 The paragraph explaining how money cards pay is in TableLegend now (BUILD-PLAN P13.5).
    It was true, and it was the same paragraph the felt and the hand were also carrying — a
    settlement is a set of numbers and the melds that produced them.
*@

<section class="settled" aria-labelledby="settled-heading">
    @*
        ⚠️ No hidden twin. "36 turns" in a pill reads correctly aloud on its own, and a .said
        saying "in 36 turns" beside it is the same fact twice — which is what a screen reader
        actually hears. Found by reading the heading's own text back out of the browser.
    *@
    <h2 id="settled-heading">
        <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">♛</span>
        <span>Round @Result.Round — @Winner went out</span>
        <span class="turns">@Result.Turns turns</span>
        @*
            §7.3: the one thing in this game paid for *how* the winner won. The nets below
            already carry it; without this the table would show a tripled round payment and
            nothing on the page would say why.
        *@
        @if (Result.Jokerless)
        {
            <span class="jokerless">jokerless — round pays ×@Multiplier</span>
        }
    </h2>

    <ol class="melds">
        @foreach (var meld in Result.Melds)
        {
            <li @key="Key(meld)">
                <span class="kind" aria-hidden="true">@DisplayTokens.For(meld.Kind)</span>
                @foreach (var slot in meld.Slots)
                {
                    <CardChip @key="slot.Card.Id.Value"
                              Card="slot.Card"
                              Token="@StandsFor(slot)"
                              TokenWords="@StandsForWords(slot)" />
                }
            </li>
        }
    </ol>

    <table>
        <caption>What each seat took home</caption>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Player</th>
                <th scope="col">Net</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var seat in Seats)
            {
                <tr @key="seat.Player.Value">
                    <th scope="row">@seat.Name@(seat.Won ? " (out)" : null)</th>
                    <td class="@Direction(Net(seat))">@Amount(Net(seat))</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>What the round settled at.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public RoundResult Result { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The seats, in seating order.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<SeatLine> Seats { get; set; } = [];

    private string Winner => Seats.FirstOrDefault(seat => seat.Player == Result.Winner)?.Name
        ?? $"Seat {Result.Winner.Value}";

    private int Net(SeatLine seat) => Result.Payouts.TryGetValue(seat.Player, out var money) ? money : 0;

    /// <summary>What a jokerless declaration is worth at this table size (RULES.md §7.3).</summary>
    private int Multiplier => TableRules.For(Seats.Count).JokerlessMultiplier;

    /// <summary>
    /// What a joker is standing in for, written after its face exactly as the console writes
    /// it — <c>🃏(4♦)</c>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <b>The interpretation is display only, never identity</b> (<c>MeldSlot</c>): the joker
    /// is still a joker, and it is the meld that decides what it is playing as here.
    /// </remarks>
    private static string? StandsFor(MeldSlot slot) => slot.IsSubstitute
        ? $"({CardText.DisplayCode(slot.PlaysAs)}{CardText.DisplaySuit(slot.InSuit)})"
        : null;

    private static string? StandsForWords(MeldSlot slot) => slot.IsSubstitute
        ? $"standing in for the {CardWords.For(Card.Ranked(slot.Card.Id, slot.PlaysAs, slot.InSuit))}"
        : null;

    /// <summary>A stable key per meld: the cards it is made of, which no other meld holds (§3.1).</summary>
    private static string Key(Meld meld) => string.Join('-', meld.CardIds.Select(id => id.Value));

    private static string Amount(int money) => money switch
    {
        > 0 => $"+${money}",
        < 0 => $"−${-money}",
        _ => "$0"
    };

    private static string Direction(int money) => money switch
    {
        > 0 => "up",
        < 0 => "down",
        _ => "level"
    };
}
